## Required Reading (Before Starting)

**ALWAYS** review these files in order:
1. `project-context.md` - Project-specific rules and patterns
2. `docs/bmad-workflow-guide.md` - Current development workflow
3. `sprint-status.yaml` - Current sprint and story status
4. This file - Beads coordination commands

---

## The Split: Who Owns What

```
BMAD (Formal Outputs):              Beads (Runtime & Coordination):
├── Documents                       ├── Work claims (bd-claim)
├── sprint-status.yaml              ├── Runtime decisions (bd-decision)
├── workflow-status.yaml            ├── Blockers (bd-blocker)
├── ADRs (architecture.md)          ├── HALTs (bd-halt)
├── Task checkboxes (story files)   ├── Cross-story dependencies
└── Code review findings            └── Action items (bd-action)
```

**Rule**: Don't duplicate. BMAD handles formal outputs. Beads handles runtime state.

---

## Session Start

```bash
bd-status              # Ready work + blockers (one command)
bd-claim "story-key"   # Claim before starting work
```

## During Work

```bash
bd-decision "title"    # Runtime decision (outside workflow)
bd-blocker "title"     # External blocker
bd-halt "reason"       # Critical failure (priority 0)
bd-action "title"      # Action item
```

## Session End

Run the `[HO]` handover workflow to safely end your session:

```bash
[HO]                   # Run handover workflow
```

Or manually:

```bash
bd-release <id>        # Release claim (if you claimed)
git add <files>        # Stage changes
git commit -m "..."    # Hooks auto-sync Beads
bd-land                # Sync all branches (beads-sync → main → current)
git push               # Push to remote
bd-status              # Report next ready work
```

> **Note**: The `[HO]` workflow handles all of this automatically. Use it to ensure proper branch sync.

